## 7. POST-INTEGRATION — evidence slots, 4 of 9 RECORDED as of 2026-09-02

### [CXC-TM1637-EV-INDEX] The evidence ledger — 4 of 9 slots filled, first bench observation 2026-09-02

- slots-total: 9
- slots-filled: 4
- hardware-status: TM1637 modules ARE connected and running production firmware, as of 2026-09-02 (glass observation, David — see EV-01, EV-02, EV-03, EV-08). Two modules are YAML-configured and actively driven, correctly and legibly, on a CLK line shared by four wired modules (the 3rd and 4th are wired but not configured, and sit inert). Basic illumination, the segment map (a-g bit order) and digit order are confirmed for the running configuration (EV-01/EV-02/EV-03) via general operation rather than the deliberate single-character protocol those slots specify — see each slot for the precise caveat. The shared-CLK / per-DIO no-cross-talk claim underlying [CXC-TM1637-SHARED-CLK] is directly supported (EV-08). [CXC-TM1637-EV-09], the deliberate negative control EV-08 depends on to mean something, has NOT been run and remains EMPTY — see its `still-needed`. EV-04 (justification), EV-05 (decimal point), EV-06 (brightness step) and EV-07 (display-off-while-writing) remain EMPTY; none were observed on this bench pass.
- why-a-human: every item here is in the class where a machine signal EXISTS and AGREES WITH THE WRONG ANSWER ([CXC-VISION-EPISTEMICS]). A wrong segment map produces confident, well-formed, incorrect glyphs that no machine signal in this system can distinguish from correct ones.
- how-to-ask: name SPECIFIC characters and state the expected result, never "does it look right". Each slot below does exactly that, and the expectation is the discriminator. Where a slot was filled from general operation rather than the scripted characters (EV-01/EV-02/EV-03/EV-08 above), the slot itself says so — a scripted re-run remains cheap and would tighten, not replace, this evidence.
- how-to-fill: replace `evidence-state: EMPTY` with `RECORDED`, fill `observed`, `observed-on-date` and `observed-by`, and leave the question and expectation untouched so the two can be compared later.
- pairing-is-load-bearing: [CXC-TM1637-EV-08] is the only test that can falsify [CXC-TM1637-SHARED-CLK], and [CXC-TM1637-EV-09] is its NEGATIVE CONTROL. Running 08 without 09 proves nothing, because a harness that is not what the tester believes produces a passing 08 for the wrong reason. As of 2026-09-02 this pairing is still incomplete: 08 is RECORDED, 09 is not — see EV-09's `corroborating-observation` for what the running config's differing-and-correct content already implies, and why it is not a substitute.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-TM1637]
- see-also: [CXC-PERIPH-EVIDENCE-SLOTS]

---

### [CXC-TM1637-EV-01] EV-01 — segment map, gross check: display `0`

- evidence-state: RECORDED
- question: display the character `0`. Are all six OUTER bars lit and the CENTRE bar DARK?
- expected: six outer bars lit, centre bar dark
- discriminates: any single wrong bar means the segment map is permuted. Note WHICH bar — that identifies the permutation rather than merely reporting failure.
- grounds-claim: [CXC-TM1637-SEGMENT-MAP-UNVERIFIED]
- observed: two TM1637 modules on the currently-running firmware correctly and legibly display their configured application values — every glyph renders as a correct, unpermuted digit shape, no garbled or half-lit character seen. This is NOT the literal scripted `0`-only test this slot specifies — no isolated `0` character was deliberately requested — it is the general operational observation that grounds the same gross-level claim: a permuted segment map would render confidently wrong glyphs, and none were seen on either module.
- observed-on-date: 2026-09-02
- observed-by: David (glass observation, currently-running firmware)
- part-of: [CXC-TM1637-EV-INDEX]

---

### [CXC-TM1637-EV-02] EV-02 — segment map, discriminating: display `1`, then `7`

- evidence-state: RECORDED
- question: display `1`, then `7`.
- expected: `1` lights the two RIGHT-HAND VERTICAL bars only; `7` adds the TOP bar
- discriminates: if `1` lights two bars on the LEFT, segments b/c are swapped with e/f. This is the check EV-01 cannot make — `0` is symmetric under exactly that swap, so a gross check passes on a permuted map.
- grounds-claim: [CXC-TM1637-SEGMENT-MAP-UNVERIFIED]
- observed: NOT the literal scripted `1`-then-`7` sequence — that isolated pair was not deliberately requested. What was observed: the running configuration's real application values, read correctly and legibly over continuous operation. Live application values on a multi-digit numeric readout necessarily include asymmetric digits (not just `0`/`8`, which are the only shapes symmetric under a b/c-e/f swap), and all rendered correctly on both modules. In substance this satisfies the discriminating condition EV-02 exists to check — a b/c-e/f swap would have shown as visibly wrong shapes on the asymmetric digits actually displayed — but it is recorded as inferred-from-general-operation rather than from the deliberate isolated-character protocol, and is weaker evidence than a scripted `1`/`7` run would be.
- observed-on-date: 2026-09-02
- observed-by: David (glass observation, currently-running firmware)
- part-of: [CXC-TM1637-EV-INDEX]

---

### [CXC-TM1637-EV-03] EV-03 — digit order: display `1234`

- evidence-state: RECORDED
- question: display `1234`. Is the LEFTMOST tube showing `1`?
- expected: leftmost tube shows `1`
- discriminates: if the leftmost shows `4`, GRID1 is the rightmost tube and the buffer needs reversing. On a 6-digit module also check for the common 2,1,0,5,4,3 scramble.
- grounds-claim: [CXC-TM1637-SEGMENT-MAP-UNVERIFIED]
- observed: NOT the literal scripted `1234` test — that specific value was not deliberately requested. What was observed: the running configuration's real multi-digit application values read left-to-right in the correct, expected order on both configured modules, with no reversed or scrambled digit positions noticed. This grounds the same claim EV-03 checks (GRID-to-tube-position mapping is correct) via the running config rather than the isolated `1234` protocol value.
- observed-on-date: 2026-09-02
- observed-by: David (glass observation, currently-running firmware)
- part-of: [CXC-TM1637-EV-INDEX]

---

### [CXC-TM1637-EV-04] EV-04 — justification: publish `42` to a 4-digit surface

- evidence-state: EMPTY
- question: publish the value `42` to a 4-digit surface. What do the four tubes show?
- expected: two BLANK tubes, then `4`, then `2` — right-justified and blank-padded
- discriminates: `42` followed by two blanks means LEFT-justified; `0042` means zero-padded. Both are well-formed and both violate [CXC-TM1637-FORMAT-BACKEND].
- grounds-claim: [CXC-TM1637-FORMAT-BACKEND]
- observed: ⛔ EMPTY
