## 8. Placement

### [CXC-TM1637-PLACEMENT] Placement is UNRATIFIED, and this directory is harder than it looks

- placement-status: UNRATIFIED. This document was written into `corpora/platform-specs/` because that is where every spec it cites already lives, NOT because the placement was ruled.
- what-makes-it-non-obvious-one: `corpora/platform-specs` is a registered root of THREE corpora at once — `intelligence-console`, `visual-composer` and `headless-monitor` all list it under `area: specs` in the corpus config. Landing a peripheral spec here puts it in all three, and a TM1637 is plausibly relevant to none of them by name.
- what-makes-it-non-obvious-two: the numeric-prefix convention has collided three times and has no guard — `00-composer-design-principles` versus `00-composer-overview`, `46-console-sources-on-the-bus` versus `46-handover-process`, and (RESOLVED 2026-08-17 by renaming to `76-fleet-console`) `61-config-over-bus` versus `61-fleet-console` ([CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT]). The filenames differ, so git produces no signal of any kind.
- what-makes-it-non-obvious-three: the next free number is not visible from a directory listing. 66, 67 and 68 were all claimed by branches in flight, and were only discoverable by enumerating branches. `69` was chosen after that enumeration; it is free on `main` and on every local branch as of 2026-08-15.
- what-makes-it-non-obvious-four: three consecutive neighbours already carry `[PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED]` — 60, 61 and 62 — which is itself the signal that the question is overdue rather than pending. This document is the fourth and does not pretend otherwise.
- the-recommendation: KEEP IT HERE as `69-tm1637-peripheral.lts`, and register a dedicated `corpora/peripherals` root ONLY when a second peripheral spec exists. A new corpus root for one document is a directory with a naming convention, not a corpus; the moment there are two, the shared vocabulary is real and the root pays for itself.
- the-alternative-worth-naming: a `peripherals` area registered in `FACTLATTICE_CORPUS_CONFIG` for whichever corpora actually consume peripherals. That is a registry edit, therefore David's, and it is the right answer if peripheral specs are expected to multiply — the TM1637 is the first of an obvious family (R503, the 4x4 keypad, the x27.168 stepper).
- second-placement-question: [CXC-PERIPH-EVIDENCE-SLOTS] is a REUSABLE pattern living inside a part-specific spec, so the next peripheral will cite into this file. Its natural home is [SPEC:CXC-BRINGUP], beside the two-tier verdict it extends. Promotion should happen when the SECOND peripheral uses it, not before — a pattern with one instance has not been shown to generalise.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-TM1637]
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT], [SPEC:CXC-BRINGUP]

